    "policyNotes": [
        {
            "topic": "Muslim festival dates",
            "text": "Muslim festivals, not falling on the notified dates due to non-sighting of moon, will be observed as per the Government guidelines. This applies to holidays marked (*): Id-ul-Fitr, Jamat-Ul-Vida, and Id-ul-Zuha (Bakrid)."
        },
        {
            "topic": "Restricted Holiday option deadline",
            "text": "For availing Restricted Holidays, concerned employees shall have to exercise their option by 31st January 2022 and obtain approval of their controlling officer before availing the same."
        },
        {
            "topic": "Compensatory Off",
            "text": "All employees (including non-executive trainees) can avail a compensatory off against not spared Closed/Public/Festival/Restricted holiday(s) within two (02) months in the same calendar year. Category A [Executives (both Works and Non-Works)], Category C [Industrial non-executives (Works & Non-Works)] and Category D (non-executive trainees) employees can avail a compensatory off against each Public/Closed holiday coinciding with their weekly off (including Sunday). Category C [industrial non-executive employee (Works & Non-Works)] employees who will not be spared, or do not want to avail Closed/Public Holidays on Republic Day, May Day, Independence Day and Mahatma Gandhi's Birthday, will have the following option: claiming Compensatory off within 2 months in the same calendar year, or Extra wages. This option is also available if any of the aforesaid holidays coincides with their weekly off (excluding Sunday); in case of Sunday weekly-off, only Compensatory off is admissible."
        },
        {
            "topic": "Proportionate RH for new joiners",
            "text": "Employees joining services of the company during the calendar year will be entitled for proportionate Restricted Holiday(s) to be calculated on half-yearly or quarterly basis with reference to their joining date, as the case may be."
        }
    ]
